id: CS-SEC-015
ilities: [integrity]
source: cpm
maturity: 2
action: block
title: Dangerous .NET deserializer usage (Exchange Server RCEs)
category: security
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .cs
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ Test/ Tests/ vendor/ .git/ build/ bin/ obj/
patterns:
  - regex: new\s+BinaryFormatter\(
    message: "BinaryFormatter is deprecated and insecure — enables RCE via gadget chains. Microsoft recommendation: never use."
  - regex: new\s+SoapFormatter\(
    message: "SoapFormatter is insecure — same RCE risks as BinaryFormatter"
  - regex: new\s+NetDataContractSerializer\(
    message: "NetDataContractSerializer is insecure — type info in payload enables RCE"
  - regex: new\s+ObjectStateFormatter\(
    message: "ObjectStateFormatter can be exploited for RCE via ViewState deserialization"
  - regex: new\s+LosFormatter\(
    message: "LosFormatter is insecure for untrusted data — ViewState deserialization RCE risk"
fix: Use System.Text.Json or DataContractSerializer. BinaryFormatter is banned by Microsoft security guidance.
